      "raw": "<p><a href=\"https://querki.net/u/darker/spirit-island-faq/#!.9v5kbjr\">https://querki.net/u/darker/spirit-island-faq/#!.9v5kbjr</a></p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>You're being told to Push 2 Dahan from a single land with a City to a single land without a City. If that's impossible, but you can Push 1 Dahan following those constraints, do so. Otherwise, do nothing on that board.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>If '1 dahan can move without city' is possible, why text didn`t contain 'up to'?</p>\r\n\r\n<p>i think it must ' must only 2 dahan move, If that's impossible impossible, this event can`t move 1 dahan.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>I'm confused because a sentence without 'up to' has the effect of including 'up to'.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>",
